## Architecture

Split frontend/backend. The Next.js / React Native apps are **thin UI clients** — all
stateful, authoritative logic lives in the Rust backend. Never embed a stateful engine
inside Next.js (route handlers and server actions are at most thin proxies to the Rust API)
or the mobile frontend.

```text
{{PROJECT_SLUG}}/
├── apps/
│   ├── web/        # Next.js frontend          (pnpm: {{PROJECT_SLUG}}-web,    port 5005)
│   └── mobile/     # React Native (Expo) app   (pnpm: {{PROJECT_SLUG}}-mobile, Expo 8081)
├── packages/       # shared internal libs (optional)
├── services/
│   └── api/        # Rust (Axum) API + business logic                          (port 7890)
├── db/             # TS DB scripts: seed.ts, prune.ts (pg node driver)
├── docs/           # PRD.md, BRANDING.md
└── docker-compose.yml   # PostgreSQL
```

Convention: `apps/*` = deployed, `packages/*` = shared libs, `services/*` = hosted backends.
Rust dirs have no `package.json` and are skipped by pnpm.

## Stack

- **Web**: Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind + React + shadcn/ui
- **Mobile**: React Native via Expo (Expo Router) + TypeScript
- **Backend**: Rust (edition 2024), Axum, SQLx (async Postgres, no ORM)
- **Auth**: roll-your-own JWT — bcrypt email/password + Sign in with Google. The backend
  issues the session token; frontends only ever hold the JWT (Bearer header).
- **DB**: PostgreSQL; schema = SQLx migrations in `services/api/migrations/`, applied on boot.

> Frameworks here may differ from your training data (Next.js, Expo, Axum, SQLx all move
> fast). Check current docs before writing framework code.

## Dev commands

```bash
pnpm dev          # api + web (concurrently)
pnpm dev:all      # api + web + mobile
pnpm dev:web      # Next.js only (port 5005)
pnpm dev:mobile   # Expo dev server
pnpm dev:api      # Rust API only (cargo run)
pnpm check        # tsc --noEmit on web
pnpm backend:test # cargo test
pnpm lint         # eslint on web
pnpm db:seed      # seed DB (tsx db/seed.ts)
pnpm db:prune     # prune DB (tsx db/prune.ts)
```

## Ports

| Service | Port |
|---|---|
| Next.js web | 5005 |
| Expo dev server | 8081 |
| Rust API | 7890 |
| PostgreSQL | 5432 |

## Environment variables

- `DATABASE_URL` — Postgres connection (backend + db scripts)
- `AUTH_SECRET` / `JWT_SECRET` — JWT signing secret
- `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` / `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI` — Sign in with Google
- `CORS_ORIGINS` — extra allowed web origins (comma-separated)
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` — engine URL for the web app (default `http://localhost:7890`)
- `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` — engine URL for the mobile app
